    regime: "The single clearest test on this board resolved overnight and the answer was that risk appetite is not what is driving it. Nvidia beat heavily - 115.8 billion dollars of revenue against about 109.3 billion expected and 2.68 dollars a share against 2.47 - and the stock rose 4% to 5% after hours, yet gold fell 1.57% to 3,789.01, silver 2.64% to 46.09, copper 2.27% to 5.84 and the yen gained against all seven other currencies. What is driving the board is the Federal Reserve: the dollar index is 103.687, its highest since April 2025, after Musalem said the United States likely needs multiple hikes before spring and Logan said at least two more quarter-point moves are required. December is 95.7% priced with 69.4% on a cumulative fifty basis points by January, and the October 28 minutes land tonight at 21:00. Underneath that, UK October CPI at 09:00 is the hour's binary, Australian wages came in hot without helping the Aussie, and the kiwi made a six-year low.",
